WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.980
In the George R.R. Martin books that HBO's
Game of Thrones is based on, the character

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.090
of Beric Dondarrion has a relatively small
part to play.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.860
But when you have an actor as talented as
Irish star Richard Dormer, you want to showcase

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.409
him as much as possible.

00:00:13.409 --> 00:00:16.800
Here's a look at some of Dormer's previous
roles to help you remember just why Beric

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.589
from Game of Thrones looks so familiar.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:20.759
Hurricane

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:24.679
Dormer got his start on the stage, appearing
in over two dozen plays.

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:29.170
In 2002, a one man play he wrote and starred
in resulted in Dormer's big break, with his

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:34.540
portrayal of controversial Irish snooker star
Alex Higgins in Hurricane garnering rave reviews

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.320
over its three-year run.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.570
Higgins himself was a fan of the play, attending
several performances and striking up a friendship

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:41.630
with Dormer.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:46.320
Following Higgins' battle with throat cancer
and subsequent death in 2010, Dormer revived

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.950
the play for a last hurrah at the Belfast
Opera House in order to give "a final farewell

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.800
to a true genius and a legend."

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.800
Hidden

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.160
In 2011, Richard Dormer landed a featured
role in the four-part BBC thriller/conspiracy

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.180
drama Hidden, starring Philip Glenister as
small-time solicitor Harry Venn.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.070
When Venn is asked to help track down the
truth about a missing witness, he finds himself

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.970
well over his head in a deep conspiracy that
may have ties to his own dark past.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.160
He enlists the help of Dormer's character
Frank Hanna, a resourceful ex-con who's out

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.920
of his depth, and finds himself in more than
one sticky situation along the way.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.480
Whatever Venn is paying him, it's definitely
not enough.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.680
Hunted

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.390
A year after his appearance in Hidden, Dormer
returned to television when he appeared in

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.020
two episodes of the Cinemax/BBC television
series Hunted, joining Game of Thrones alumni

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.570
Stephen Dillane and Indira Varma in the production.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.840
Dormer played venture capitalist Lewis Conroy,
who is present during a murder committed by

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.100
his business partner, Jack Turner.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.612
Conroy later attempts to track down the woman
who witnessed their crime in order to find

00:01:49.612 --> 00:01:52.310
out exactly how much she knows.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:53.310
Good Vibrations

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:58.850
In 2013, Dormer teamed up with yet another
Game of Thrones co-star — Liam Cunningham

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:03.770
— for a dramedy based on the life of Belfast
record-store owner Terri Hooley, founder of

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.750
the "Good Vibrations" record store.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:09.929
Set during the height of the violent "Troubles"
in the 1970s, Good Vibrations finds Hooley

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:13.909
opening his Belfast shop on "the most bombed
half-mile in Europe."

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:18.569
After hearing some up-and-coming underground
punk bands, Hooley embraces the new art form,

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:20.529
inspiring to start his own record label.

00:02:20.529 --> 00:02:25.620
Good Vibrations gained wide critical acclaim,
bringing Dormer a Best Actor nomination at

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.650
the Irish Film and Television Awards.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:34.669
"It's showing you know, a sense of people
rising above and against something that's

00:02:34.669 --> 00:02:35.669
ultimately dark."

00:02:35.669 --> 00:02:36.799
'71

00:02:36.799 --> 00:02:42.629
In 2014, Dormer starred in another film about
the Troubles when he appeared in the historical

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.180
thriller '71.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.180
When a unit of the British Army is deployed
to Belfast, they find themselves stationed

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.959
in a dangerous neighborhood with Catholics
on one side and Protestants on the other.

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:56.919
Under attack from both sides, they're forced
to withdraw, accidentally leaving one soldier

00:02:56.919 --> 00:02:57.980
behind.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.790
Dormer plays a Catholic man who helps the
soldier, putting his daughter's life in grave

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:02.790
danger.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:03.790
We're Doomed!

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.279
The Dad's Army Story

00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:11.310
Created in 1968 by Jimmy Perry and David Croft,
the sitcom Dad's Army focused on a fictional

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.480
group of British Home Guard soldiers during
World War II.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.120
The show became one of the U.K.'s most beloved
comedies, running for 80 episodes and spawning

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.049
two different movie adaptations.

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:25.780
In 2015, the BBC premiered a TV movie about
the making of the series called We're Doomed!

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.970
The Dad's Army Story, with Richard Dormer
playing the series' co-creator, David Croft.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.629
11 Minutes

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:37.120
Also in 2015, Richard Dormer starred as a
sleazy Hollywood director in the Polish experimental

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.999
action movie 11 Minutes.

00:03:38.999 --> 00:03:43.019
The film chronicles the lives of a number
of Warsaw residents, including a low-level

00:03:43.019 --> 00:03:48.629
drug runner, an elderly artist, a hot-dog
vendor, a skyscraper window washer, a student,

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:52.359
a team of paramedics, and an actress and her
jealous husband.

00:03:52.359 --> 00:03:56.120
As director Richard Martin holds an "audition"
for the actress in a hotel room, the rest

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.890
of the characters go about their lives.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:04.359
But for 11 minutes, their paths all intersect
in unexpected and life-changing ways.

00:04:04.359 --> 00:04:05.359
Fortitude

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:10.559
2015 continued to be a busy year for the actor,
as that's when Dormer got his own starring

00:04:10.559 --> 00:04:15.079
television role in the Amazon Original series
Fortitude, playing Sheriff Dan Anderssen,

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:17.910
the man charged with protecting the residents
of an isolated town.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.699
The town of Fortitude is historically

00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:20.699
peaceful.

00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:24.650
But that all changes when a local scientist
is found brutally murdered — the first violent

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:26.400
crime in the town's history.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.490
"This would not stop me, nevermind a bear."

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:34.490
Unbeknownst to Anderssen, one of the town's
residents has placed a call resulting in the

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:39.620
arrival of London Police Inspector Eugene
Morton, who comes to Fortitude to "help" with

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.979
the investigation.

00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:44.420
The show has run for two seasons thus far,
with fellow Game of Thrones alumni Michelle

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.639
Fairley joining the cast in season two.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:47.639
Thanks for watching!

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:50.090
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.560
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

